Z||000000||Lynx||10-04-1999||01:16 AM||||Ok my 85 V6 is in trouble. The thing started before and wont know. First the fuel pump wasnt coming on so i bypassed the relay and hot wired it. Boom i have fuel presure but it still wont start. I do have spark and it kinda fired a few times. Heres the thing i was checking the relay to the fuel pump and the hot wire is good and the ground is good but when i turn on the key the wire form the ECM to the relay has no power. So im wondering if i have ECM problems because even with fuel pressure still no run.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Zzaaak||10-04-1999||03:54 AM||||Sounds like the problem I just had.  Looks like you just might need a new fuel pump.  You might have your fuel pressure after you hot wired the fuel pump.  But the thing is if your fuel presure isn't high enough must be around 40 psi.  Your car is not going to run.  Or it might spit and sputter and run terrible at low RPM's.  I just put a new fuel pump in my 87 fiero yesterday... It has 127,000 miles on it.... Maybe thats the time fuel pumps go out.   Depending on how long your car has been sitting your gas can be varnished.  If the fuel pump isn't it could be the fuel presure regulator.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Lynx||10-05-1999||04:26 AM||||It wont start at all not really even firing. The thing that really bugs me the point that the ECM is not throughing a signal to the relay to turn it on.||||reg||9
Z||000003||Formula||10-05-1999||06:19 PM||||You just ginxed my car. Today after school I ran out of gas in the parking lot. I thought it was the fuel pump but put gas in it anyways. My gauge is broken and there was only 90 miles on it since the last refill. well, anyways it started right up with gas. But your comment on the 127000 mile fuel pump is off cause mine has 135000 on it. But like I said, Its ginxed now.||||reg||1
Z||000004||SloPonti||10-05-1999||07:18 PM||||a while back ago my car was running and then all of a sudden it shut off! i would try to start it and it would almost start and then shut off! i then replaced the fuel pump and it still did not work! i had spark sometimes and other times i did not-next part to replace was the ecm-i tried to pull the codes and you should get a code 12 but i did not even have that-next i pulled the ecm out and pulled the cover off of it and you could see some of the electrical parts in there were melted and they smelled burnt also-i then replaced it and everything has worked fine every since!||||reg||5
Z||000005||Lynx||10-06-1999||02:15 AM||||And how much did that new ECM cost you i bet they are real spendy.||||reg||9
